---
import HubFooter from "../../../../components/aopa/HubFooter.astro";
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
	<meta charset="utf-8" />
	<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
	<title>Human Factors: Spatial Disorientation and Decision Making | AOPA</title>
	<meta
		name="description"
		content="Human factors resources for general aviation pilots: run your IMSAFE checklist, judge your fitness to fly, and learn to recognize spatial disorientation."
	/>
</head>
<body>

<div class="home">
	<header class="home__header" id="home-header">
		<img class="home__chrome" src="/images/aopa/home/1/chrome-100.jpg" alt="" />
		<img class="home__mini-nav" src="/images/aopa/home/1/mini-nav-100.jpg" alt="" />
	</header>

	<section class="js-hub-hero hub-hero relative overflow-hidden bg-white">
		<div class="flex min-h-[calc(60vh-var(--chrome-h))] flex-col lg:flex-row">
			<div class="relative flex w-full flex-col justify-center lg:w-1/2">
				<p class="absolute left-0 top-0 px-8 pt-8 font-national font-light text-[#182f56]/80 sm:px-12 lg:px-16">
					<a href="/" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:underline">Home</a>
					<span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
					<a href="/aopa/hub/safety" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:underline">Safety</a>
					<span aria-hidden="true">›</span> Human Factors
				</p>
				<div class="mx-auto max-w-xl px-8 py-12 sm:px-12 lg:px-16">
					<p class="font-national text-2xl font-extrabold uppercase tracking-wide text-[#777777] sm:text-2xl">
						Human Factors
					</p>
					<h1 class="mt-2 max-w-[16ch] font-national font-extrabold text-4xl leading-[1.05] tracking-tight text-gray-800 sm:text-5xl">
						A safe flight starts and ends with the pilot
					</h1>
					<p class="mt-5 max-w-[42ch] font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-500 sm:text-2xl">
						From the runup to the rollout, these human factors and spatial disorientation
						resources help you manage your body, mind, and judgment.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="relative min-h-[360px] w-full overflow-hidden lg:min-h-0 lg:w-1/2">
				<img
					class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 h-full w-full select-none object-cover"
					src="/images/aopa/hub/safety/23_eFIRC3079-cropped.jpg"
					alt=""
				/>
				<div
					class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 bottom-0 h-1/2 bg-[linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(13,27,42,0)_0%,rgba(13,27,42,0.45)_100%)]"
					aria-hidden="true"
				></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== INTRO ===== -->
	<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#2b2b2e] px-8 py-20 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl">
			<p class="font-national text-xl font-light sm:leading-[1.6] text-white sm:text-2xl">
				The AOPA Air Safety Institute's human factors resources help general aviation pilots
				sharpen aeronautical decision making, assess their own fitness to fly, recognize spatial
				disorientation, and survive a forced landing. The Do the Right Thing course is eligible
				for both Federal Aviation Administration (FAA) Wings credit and Accident Forgiveness and
				is free to all pilots. In Safety Spotlights, pilots share lessons learned from the
				cockpit.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== EXPLORE BY TOPIC ===== -->
	<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gray-100 px-8 py-24 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl">
			<div class="mb-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-8">
				<h2 class="max-w-[16ch] font-national text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-800 sm:text-4xl">
					Explore human factors by topic
				</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
				<a href="#" class="relative isolate flex min-h-[200px] flex-col justify-start gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg bg-white p-7 no-underline">
					<div class="relative">
						<span class="block font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Make better go/no-go calls</span>
						<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-gray-600">
							Improve your aeronautical decision making with the Do the Right Thing spotlight and
							course. Set personal minimums with ready-made contracts, spot the external pressures
							pushing a flight, and build habits that keep tough calls from sneaking up on you.
						</p>
					</div>
					<span class="mt-3 inline-block font-national text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#01a2e0]">Aeronautical Decision Making →</span>
				</a>
				<a href="#" class="relative isolate flex min-h-[200px] flex-col justify-start gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white p-7 no-underline">
					<div class="relative">
						<span class="block font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Mental health help, no judgment</span>
						<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-gray-600">
							The Mental Health Resource Center offers helpful videos, including one with the
							federal air surgeon on medical certification, an interactive stress scale, quick
							links to FAA mental health guides and myth busters, and a crisis line you can call,
							text, or chat.
						</p>
					</div>
					<span class="mt-3 inline-block font-national text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#01a2e0]">Mental Health Resource Center →</span>
				</a>
				<a href="#" class="relative isolate flex min-h-[200px] flex-col justify-start gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white p-7 no-underline">
					<div class="relative">
						<span class="block font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Check your fitness to fly</span>
						<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-gray-600">
							Self-assess before every flight, the same way you preflight the airplane. The
							Aeromedical Center's Aging Gracefully and Fighting Fatigue Safety Spotlights help you
							judge age- and rest-related changes, so you can stay proficient and fly ready.
						</p>
					</div>
					<span class="mt-3 inline-block font-national text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#01a2e0]">Aeromedical →</span>
				</a>
				<a href="#" class="relative isolate flex min-h-[200px] flex-col justify-start gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white p-7 no-underline">
					<div class="relative">
						<span class="block font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">When your senses lie</span>
						<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-gray-600">
							Spatial disorientation can take hold fast when you lose the horizon. Learn the
							illusions that fool the body, how bank rates can go undetected, and tips for night
							flying over water. Accident case studies offer cautionary tales for your checklist.
						</p>
					</div>
					<span class="mt-3 inline-block font-national text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#01a2e0]">Spatial Disorientation →</span>
				</a>
				<a href="#" class="relative isolate flex min-h-[200px] flex-col justify-start gap-3 overflow-hidden rounded-lg border border-black/5 bg-white p-7 no-underline">
					<div class="relative">
						<span class="block font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Survive after a forced landing</span>
						<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-gray-600">
							Walking away is only the start. Learn how to brief passengers, what gear to carry,
							and how to stay alive after an off-airport landing in the Survive: Beyond the Forced
							Landing Safety Spotlight. Find the post-accident sequence and more at this safety
							center.
						</p>
					</div>
					<span class="mt-3 inline-block font-national text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#01a2e0]">Survival Safety →</span>
				</a>
			</div>

			<p class="mt-8 font-national text-xl text-gray-600">
				Running a flight school or operation?
				<a href="#" class="font-bold text-[#01a2e0] no-underline hover:underline">See the Scalable Safety Framework →</a>
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== REAL PILOT STORIES AND EXPERT INSIGHTS ===== -->
	<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white px-8 py-24 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">
			<div class="flex flex-col gap-10 lg:flex-row lg:items-start lg:justify-between">
				<div class="max-w-[60ch]">
					<h2 class="font-national text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-800 sm:text-4xl">
						Hear it from pilots who were there
					</h2>
					<p class="mt-4 pr-6 font-national text-lg font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-600 sm:text-2xl">
						In Real Pilot Stories, pilots share what went wrong and how they recovered. Expert
						Insights courses go deeper, led by people who know the subject, from an Air Force
						neurologist to a Coast Guard pilot.
					</p>
				</div>

				<div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-4 lg:w-1/2">
					<a href="#" class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-black/10 bg-gray-100 px-7 py-6 no-underline">
						<span class="font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Real Pilot Stories</span>
						<span class="font-national text-xl font-bold text-[#01a2e0]">→</span>
					</a>
					<a href="#" class="flex items-center justify-between rounded-lg border border-black/10 bg-gray-100 px-7 py-6 no-underline">
						<span class="font-national text-xl font-medium text-gray-800">Expert Insights</span>
						<span class="font-national text-xl font-bold text-[#01a2e0]">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== STORYTELLING AND PROOF + AOPA IN ACTION ===== -->
	<section class="js-hub-advocacy relative overflow-hidden bg-[#1d3f6d] px-8 py-36 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<img
			class="js-hub-advocacy-bg pointer-events-none absolute inset-x-0 -top-[100%] h-[300%] w-full select-none object-cover will-change-transform"
			src="/images/aopa/home/4/sky-portrait.jpg"
			alt=""
		/>
		<div class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 bg-[#1d3f6d]/55"></div>

		<div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl">
			<div class="js-reveal mb-14 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
				<div class="mr-12">
					<h2 class="max-w-[32ch] font-national text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">
						Judgment is a skill you can build
					</h2>
					<p class="mt-6 max-w-[60ch] font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-white/90">
						Risk is personal. Every pilot brings a unique mix of experience, knowledge, skill, and
						proficiency to the cockpit; operations that are perfectly safe for one pilot may be
						hazardous for another. That's why these resources help you measure your own limits,
						not a generic standard. Know your own limits before you fly and honor them.
					</p>
				</div>
				<blockquote class="max-w-[42ch] font-national text-3xl font-light italic leading-snug text-white">
					"Safe so far does not translate into safe forever."
					<footer class="mt-2 font-national text-xl not-italic font-light text-white/60">
						Justin Moore, U.S. Coast Guard pilot, Expert Insights: Risk Management
					</footer>
				</blockquote>
			</div>

			<div class="js-reveal mb-20 grid grid-cols-1 gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
				<div>
					<div class="font-national text-4xl font-bold text-[#7ce0ff]">40 minutes</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-white/90">
						to complete the Do the Right Thing course
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<div class="font-national text-4xl font-bold text-[#7ce0ff]">7 chapters</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-white/90">
						in the Spatial Disorientation: Confusion Kills spotlight
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<div class="font-national text-4xl font-bold text-[#7ce0ff]">5</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-white/90">
						Expert Insights video courses
					</p>
				</div>
				<div>
					<div class="font-national text-4xl font-bold text-[#7ce0ff]">5</div>
					<p class="mt-2 font-national text-xl font-light text-white/90">
						FAA resources in the Mental Health Resource Center
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<div class="js-reveal grid gap-10 rounded-lg bg-[#0d1b2a]/50 p-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center">
				<div>
					<div class="mb-3 font-national font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#7ce0ff]">
						AOPA in Action
					</div>
					<h3 class="max-w-[26ch] font-national text-2xl font-extrabold text-white">
						A mental health bill clears the Senate
					</h3>
					<p class="mt-4 max-w-[52ch] font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-white/90">
						On September 24, 2026, the U.S. Senate passed the John A. Hauser Mental Health in
						Aviation Act, work AOPA has long pushed for. AOPA served on the FAA rulemaking
						committee behind it. If enacted, it would revise FAA rules to encourage pilots to
						seek help and disclose mental health conditions and require regular special
						issuance reviews. The final bill is expected by December 31.
					</p>
					<a
						href="#"
						class="mt-5 inline-flex items-center gap-2 font-national text-lg font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#7ce0ff] no-underline"
					>
						Read AOPA's report on the Senate vote →
					</a>
					<p class="mt-4 font-national text-sm font-light text-white/50">
						Source: AOPA News and Media, September 2026
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="js-hub-advocacy-photo relative min-h-[280px] overflow-hidden rounded-lg">
					<img
						src="/images/aopa/hub/template/two-pilots.jpg"
						alt=""
						class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 h-full w-full select-none object-cover"
					/>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== MEMBER BENEFIT PROMPT ===== -->
	<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-white px-8 py-24 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center">
			<h3 class="font-national text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-800">
				Pilots look out for each other; AOPA is how that happens at scale
			</h3>
			<p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-[50ch] font-national text-2xl font-light text-gray-500">
				Our safety resources are free. Membership adds tools like flight planning, the pilot
				helpline, and publications, and puts your weight behind our work to defend your right to
				fly.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- ===== FAQ + CROSS-LINKS + PROVENANCE ===== -->
	<section class="relative overflow-hidden bg-[#f2f2f2] px-8 py-24 sm:px-12 lg:px-24">
		<div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-24 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_1fr] lg:gap-x-64">
			<div>
				<h2 class="mb-8 font-national text-3xl font-extrabold text-gray-800">
					Questions Pilots Ask
				</h2>

				<div class="js-faq border-t border-[#182f56]/10">
				<div class="js-faq-item is-open border-b border-[#182f56]/10">
					<button type="button" class="js-faq-q flex w-full items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left text-xl font-national text-base font-bold text-[#182f56]">
						What is aeronautical decision making?
						<span class="js-faq-plus font-national text-xl font-light text-[#01a2e0]">+</span>
					</button>
					<div class="js-faq-a overflow-hidden">
						<p class="mb-5 font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
							Aeronautical decision making is the systematic way a pilot assesses a situation and
							chooses the safest course of action. The AOPA Air Safety Institute teaches it
							through the Do the Right Thing course, covering the accident chain, personal
							minimums, external pressure, and contingency planning. See
							<a href="#" class="text-[#01a2e0] no-underline hover:underline">Aeronautical Decision Making</a>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="js-faq-item border-b border-[#182f56]/10">
					<button type="button" class="js-faq-q flex w-full text-xl items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left font-national text-base font-bold text-[#182f56]">
						What is spatial disorientation and how do I recover?
						<span class="js-faq-plus font-national text-xl font-light text-[#01a2e0]">+</span>
					</button>
					<div class="js-faq-a overflow-hidden">
						<p class="mb-5 font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
							Spatial disorientation is losing track of your aircraft's attitude, altitude, or
							motion when you lose visual cues like a clear view of the horizon. To recover,
							trust your instruments and not what your body is telling you, then level the wings
							and transition to instrument flight. See
							<a href="#" class="text-[#01a2e0] no-underline hover:underline">Spatial Disorientation</a>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="js-faq-item border-b border-[#182f56]/10">
					<button type="button" class="js-faq-q flex w-full items text-xl items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left font-national  font-bold text-[#182f56]">
						Can instrument-rated pilots become spatially disoriented?
						<span class="js-faq-plus font-national text-xl font-light text-[#01a2e0]">+</span>
					</button>
					<div class="js-faq-a overflow-hidden">
						<p class="mb-5 font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
							An instrument rating is no guarantee against spatial disorientation; even
							experienced, instrument-rated pilots can lose orientation in clouds or at night and
							must rely on their instruments and training to recover. This spotlight shows how it
							happens and how to stay ahead of it. See
							<a href="#" class="text-[#01a2e0] no-underline hover:underline">Spatial Disorientation</a>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
				<div class="js-faq-item border-b border-[#182f56]/10">
					<button type="button" class="js-faq-q flex w-full items text-xl items-center justify-between gap-4 py-5 text-left font-national  font-bold text-[#182f56]">
						Which human factors resources earn FAA Wings credit?
						<span class="js-faq-plus font-national text-xl font-light text-[#01a2e0]">+</span>
					</button>
					<div class="js-faq-a overflow-hidden">
						<p class="mb-5 font-national text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-gray-500">
							Do the Right Thing earns FAA Wings credit, as do three Expert Insights courses:
							Survival Equipment, Risk Management, and Crash Considerations. To enroll, select
							"Take the Course" and create a free AOPA login. Safety Spotlights do not earn FAA
							Wings credit. See
							<a href="#" class="text-[#01a2e0] no-underline hover:underline">Aeronautical Decision Making</a>.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			</div>

			<div class="flex flex-col gap-10">
				<div>
					<p class="font-national font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-[#182f56]">
						Elsewhere on aopa.org
					</p>
					<ul class="mt-4 list-none space-y-2 p-0 font-national text-lg text-[#182f56]">
						<li><a href="/aopa/hub/safety" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Safety</a></li>
						<li><a href="#" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Safety → AOPA Air Safety Institute</a></li>
						<li><a href="#" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Safety → Accident Analysis → Night Flying Accident Report</a></li>
						<li><a href="#" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Safety → Weather → VFR into IMC</a></li>
						<li><a href="#" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Safety → Flight Operations → Emergency Procedures</a></li>
						<li><a href="#" class="text-[#182f56] no-underline hover:text-[#01a2e0]">Go Fly → Medical Resources</a></li>
					</ul>
				</div>

				<p class="border-t border-[#182f56]/10 pt-6 font-national text-sm font-light text-gray-500">
					Reviewed by the AOPA Air Safety Institute (reviewers named) · Last updated [DATE]
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<HubFooter />
</div>

<style>
	@font-face {
		font-family: "National";
		src: url("/fonts/test-national-extrabold.woff2") format("woff2");
		font-weight: 800;
		font-style: normal;
		font-display: swap;
	}

	@font-face {
		font-family: "National";
		src: url("/fonts/test-national-extrabold-italic.woff2") format("woff2");
		font-weight: 800;
